description:
Read a `emem:fact:<cell64>:<fact_cid>` citation handle and return the reading that it cites. `value`, `unit`, `band` and `kind` are at the TOP level of the answer, beside the full signed `fact` body. You do not split the token or call `GET /v1/facts/<cid>` yourself. Memory algebra: the `resolve` operation (https://emem.dev/docs/model.html).

When to use: Call this when you have a memory_token from another agent or an earlier turn and need the value. For a scalar, quote `value_verbatim`, the exact decimal string that the responder signed. A null `value` or `unit` means the fact has none (an absence, or an index with no unit). It does not mean a missing field. A cid that this responder does not hold returns a typed 404. Then try /v1/fetch, or resolve at a mirror.

Example arguments: {"token":"emem:fact:defi.zb493.xoso.zcb6a:cxjiu7l54ujzrpnekp24n4534yojpue4mprddbvevnqtti3lh5bq"}
